SHADOW CLONE JUTSU — CHAKRA COST REFERENCE (downloaded, source: academy forum thread)

Regular Clone Jutsu (academy-taught): near-zero chakra cost, illusion only,
no physical substance. This is what you're SUPPOSED to use for the exam.

Shadow Clone Jutsu (Kage Bunshin): real physical clones, but each one splits
your total chakra pool. Most shinobi can only make a handful before running
dry — this is why it's classified as a high-level/forbidden-scroll technique
for regular students.

Note: some people have chakra reserves large enough that this isn't really a
limiting factor for them. If that's you, congratulations, you've been using
the "advanced" technique as your day-one basic move without realizing it was
supposed to be hard. Don't mention this to the instructor, it apparently
causes a whole conversation about "how" and "why" that takes forever.

Bonus use: each clone experiencing something transfers that memory back on
dispersal. Good for training multiple approaches to the same problem at once,
or covering more ground on recon-type tasks.
